"**Bodil\u2019s Gap \u2013 554 pages**\n\nAmong all of Brazen\u202fHead\u202fGames\u2019 published role\u2011playing books, the campaign setting *Bodil\u2019s Gap* (released on DriveThruRPG in 2021) is by far the longest, clocking in at **554 pages**.  \n\nOther titles from the same publisher are much shorter \u2013 for example, *Core\u202fDecay* (the indie cyber\u2011punk/first\u2011person RPG) is only about 18 pages long, and the various quick\u2011start playbooks or shortstories in the Bodil\u2019s Gap line are only a few dozen pages each. No other Brazen\u202fHead Games product exceeds the 554\u2011page mark, so *Bodil\u2019s Gap* holds the title of the longest book in their RPG catalog."